meta {
  name: 06 Upsert Result Values
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/results
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "values": [
      {
        "resultParamId": "{{resultParamId}}",
        "observed1": "1.1",
        "observed2": "",
        "unit": "mg/dL",
        "methodology": "Enzymatic",
        "referenceRangeId": "{{referenceRangeId}}",
        "referenceDisplay": "0.6 - 1.3 mg/dL"
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Bulk upsert result values on the Test Entry grid (LABORATORY.docx §4.3).
  Does NOT change the report's status — call Save or Submit afterward. One
  row per `resultParamId`; re-sending the same id updates it in place.

  Dynamic/calculated parameters (`parameterType = CALCULATED` on the test's
  result params) are re-evaluated authoritatively from their formula AFTER this
  upsert, over the report's current values, and stored with `source = CALCULATED`
  (dependency chains evaluate in order). To keep a manual override on a
  calculated parameter, send it with `"isManualOverride": true` — it is then
  stored with `source = MANUAL` and left out of the recompute until reset.
  A formula that can't be computed yet (blank/non-numeric input, division by
  zero) blanks that slot rather than failing the save.

  **Analyzer (machine) values.** A value an analyzer filled (`source = ADAPTER`,
  `enteredBy` = the analyzer's id) STAYS the analyzer's after a Save when Observed 1
  and Observed 2 are unchanged (trimmed; empty equals null; the unit is not
  compared). Only the range id, display text and method are then updated (the unit
  only when the analyzer sent none). A changed value becomes `MANUAL` (the
  technician), and each overwrite is recorded in the report's Audit Trail
  (`GET /lab-reports/:id/history`, action `ANALYZER_VALUE_OVERWRITTEN`, with the old
  and new value and the analyzer's name).
  - `overridesAnalyzer` (optional boolean): the technician confirmed overwriting the
    analyzer's value or range. Forces `MANUAL` even when the number is unchanged
    (e.g. only the range was changed).
  - `loadedUpdatedAt` (optional ISO date): the value's `updatedAt` as the screen loaded
    it. If the stored analyzer value has changed since (the analyzer re-sent a result
    while the screen was open) the whole save is refused with 409
    `LAB_REPORT_VALUE_CHANGED` and nothing is written; reload and review. Omit it to
    skip the check.
  Both fields are optional; older clients that omit them keep working. Unknown
  fields are rejected (400), so deploy the backend before a frontend that sends them.

  **Report highlighting (QUALITATIVE / SEMI_QUANTITATIVE only).** The Test Entry
  grid lets the technician highlight a categorical parameter's observed value(s)
  on the generated report:
  - `highlightInReport` (optional boolean, default false): when true, this
    parameter's Observed 1 and Observed 2 render in the chosen style on the report.
  - `highlightLogic` (optional enum, `AbnormalFlag`): which style to apply — only
    `BOLD_AND_RED` is offered in the UI today. Read only when `highlightInReport`
    is true.
  These are honoured for qualitative/semi-quantitative parameters only; for a
  quantitative parameter they are ignored by the print builder (its out-of-range
  values are flagged automatically from the numeric reference range instead).

  404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND`. 409 `LAB_REPORT_LOCKED` if the report is locked.
  409 `LAB_REPORT_VALUE_CHANGED` if an analyzer value changed since `loadedUpdatedAt`.
}
